<title>JAPAN: Present forex rate positive for Japan--MITI quoted.</title>
<headline>Present forex rate positive for Japan--MITI quoted.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The present level of foreign exchange rates has more positive than negative aspects for Japanese industry, Jiji news agency quoted Vice Trade Minister Tsutomu Makino as saying on Monday.  </p>
<p>Asked about recent movements in the currency market, Makino was quoted as saying: &quot;At the present level, there are more positive aspects for Japanese industry.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that an increase in Japanese exports of cars was unlikely to trigger trade friction with other nations.</p>
</text>
